AI System Integration Testing and Quality Validation Plan (Groups B–F)
For Groups B–F, the responsibility is treated as AI System Integration Testing and Quality Validation, rather than conventional API testing alone.
Objectives
Establish that:
￼ The Vector Database contains the right information and retrieves the right context.
￼ RAG combines Knowledge Graph and Vector Database context correctly.
￼ The LLM generates accurate, complete, and source-grounded answers.
￼ MCP exposes the correct functionality to external AI applications.
￼ The complete workflow works reliably across document batches, including reprocessing and updates.
1. Overall System Testing Approach
Execute the work in this sequence:
System Testing Execution Sequence
￼ B — Vector Database Validation: Establish that chunks, embeddings, and metadata are correct.
￼ C — RAG Functional & AI Quality: Establish that retrieval and generated answers are accurate and grounded.
￼ D — MCP Integration: Establish that MCP clients can discover and invoke tools correctly.
￼ E — End-to-End Integration: Validate the entire document-to-answer workflow.
￼ F — Reconciliation & ST Sign-off: Consolidate evidence, quality measurements, defects, and acceptance results.
2. Detailed Testing Plan for Each Workstream
Group B — Vector Database Validation
Objective: Confirm that the vector database has the right chunks, metadata, and embeddings, and that relevant information can be retrieved for a given question.
Test Execution Plan
Test Activity
How to Perform It
Expected Result
Record count validation
Compare expected chunk count with vector record count
Counts reconcile or differences are explained
Metadata validation
